      "message": "fix(sim): verify refuses a non-finite or zero tool axis and normalises a scaled one\n\nThe NonFinite law checked a move's from/to but not its tool axis: an\naxis like [1e-12, 0, inf] read as tilted and the reach law convicted\nnothing, and a 7x-scaled axis lost its ShankHit because reach reads\na[2] as a unit component.\n\nverify now passes the path through one door (verify/axis_door.rs)\nbefore any law: a non-finite, zero-length or overflowing axis is\nrefused by Warning::NonFinite (kept as stated, so each law's own guard\nstill fires), and a finite axis off unit length by more than 1e-12 in\n|a|^2 is normalised once in a copy the laws read. Unit axes pass bit\nfor bit through a borrowed Cow, so no existing verdict moves.\n\nPinned by tests/axis_door.rs (both reproductions); radial_rapids'\nzero-axis test now also expects the NonFinite refusal.\n\nFixes #1312\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>",
